## Lore

The Imprimer is a medium-assault unit built with speed, agility and
reconnaissance in mind as well as full infantry capability, and these cyborgs
are typically assigned to infantry, scouting, intelligence and recce positions.

The body styling carries a variety of weapons along with removable cyborg armor,
and the bionic body is strong, fast and agile. Standard colouring is matte black
plating accented in light greyish-green, and the face plate has a stern,
featureless robot look with white or yellow eyes, the top of the helmet crowned
with two or three spikes.

Underneath the cold mechanical features one typically finds the soldier''s
original human face and hair, or a human-looking facsimile. The book gives the
reason plainly: it has been found that keeping a normal looking face helps the
soldier stay in touch with his humanity.

## GM Notes

Every Free Quebec cyborg soldier is fitted with amplified hearing and a sound
filtration system, to filter out the noise of combat and to buffer the sonic
booms of the Boom Guns. They suffer no combat penalty even standing right next
to a Glitter Boy.

Standard military issue is all the appropriate ammunition and equipment for the
Borg''s body styling and weapon systems, an energy rifle of choice, four extra
E-Clips, four grenades of choice, utility belt, backpack, a walkie-talkie for
back-up, and regular maintenance and repairs. The character has medium security
clearance to most Free Quebec military bases, hospitals and facilities.

Standard military ranking, private to general. Additional bionics and
cybernetics may be added as a reward or for a special mission, drawn from Rifts,
Rifts Triax and the NGR, or Rifts Underseas.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fq-cyborg-imprimer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
